%T A006159 16,16,16,16,17,18,19,19,20,20,21,22,23,23,23,24,24,24,24,24,25,25,26,
%U A006159 27,27,28,29
%N A006159 a(n) = a(a(n-4)) + a(n-a(n-4)).
%D A006159 J. Arkin, D. C. Arney, L. S. Dewald and W. E. Ebel, Jr., Families of recursive sequences, J. Rec. Math., 22 (No. 22, 1990), 85-94.
%D A006159 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A006159 Benoit Cloitre, <a href="/A006159/b006159.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A006159 Benoit Cloitre, <a href="/A006159/a006159.pdf">Growth of A006159</a>
%H A006159 Benoit Cloitre, <a href="/A006159/a006159.png">Plot of (a(n)/n-1/2)*sqrt(log(n)) for n=1 up to 10^8</a>
%F A006159 a(n) = n/2 + O(n/sqrt(log(n))) so that lim_{n->oo} a(n)/n = 1/2. Also, a(126*2^k) = 63*2^k and a(126*2^k + 1) = 63*2^k + 1 for k >= 0. - _Benoit Cloitre_, Oct 11 2026
